# Use an adaptive three-phase policy: spend a substantial free-form setup budget first, then open a single verified answer span, then grow a compact arithmetic expression under grammar control until it is complete and long enough to avoid truncation. The control uses multiple signals: setup length, remaining budget, parser completion state, extendability, and constrained answer length.
